# Ant Design UI (required)

All client UI must use **Ant Design (`antd`)** components. Do not invent custom list rows, table markup, form wrappers, or steppers when antd already provides them.

## Required mappings

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Data lists (desktop) | `Table` |
| Data lists (mobile) | `Card` stack + `Pagination` |
| Forms | `Form` + `Form.useForm()` + `Form.Item` `name`/`rules` — **not** `react-hook-form` / `Controller` |
| Multi-step flows | `Steps` (+ optional `Progress`) — **not** custom progress bars/dots |
| Modals, buttons, inputs, selects, uploads, tags, empty, pagination | antd equivalents |
| Icons | `@ant-design/icons` |

## Lists

- **Desktop (`md+`)**: antd `Table` with `columns`, `rowKey`, `loading`, `pagination`.
- **Mobile (`< md`)**: antd `Card` list + `Pagination` / `Empty` / `Spin` — hide the table with CSS.
- Put actions with `Button`, `Space`, `Tooltip`, `Popconfirm`.
- Do **not** build HTML/CSS “fake tables” (header row + mapped row divs).

## Forms

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — RHF wrapping antd
const { control } = useForm();
<Controller name="name" control={control} render={({ field }) => <Input {...field} />} />

// ✅ GOOD — antd Form
const [form] = Form.useForm();
<Form form={form} layout="vertical" onFinish={onSubmit}>
  <Form.Item name="name" label={t('…')} rules={[{ required: true, message: t('validation.required') }]}>
    <Input />
  </Form.Item>
</Form>
```

## Steppers

Use `Steps` for navigation. Optional `Progress` for percent complete. No custom `.mobileDot` / track markup.

## Allowed outside antd

- Page layout chrome (header title, page SCSS spacing)
- React Query / routing / i18n / domain logic
- Co-located SCSS that **styles** antd components (className on `Table`/`Card`/`Form`/`Modal`)
